                <pb facs="0382" n="302" sameAs="frus:frus1901/pg302"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Adee to Mr.
                            Iddings.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1901-08-01"><hi rendition="#italic">August 1,
                        1901</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Adee states that Mr. Iddings’s testimony may be given on terms consistent
                    with representative dignity. Unless interrogatory in open court is
                    indispensable, personal deposition at the embassy is preferable.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
